<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Veda Butte (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:151-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019331); confidence: high; pdf_page: 143; book_elev_ft: 3830</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280208" lon="-121.733236"><ele>1103.1</ele><name>Airstrip junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_142-2: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Road NF 2656 and NF 2650-131; confidence: high; pdf_page: 144; book_elev_ft: 3600</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286242" lon="-121.737580"><ele>1117.5</ele><name>Pioneer Graves junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_142-2: OSM junction of East Chimney Rock Road and NF 2650-131; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 145</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280905" lon="-121.741343"><ele>1137.8</ele><name>Westside Divide</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Sherar Burn Road NF 2613 and Still Creek Road NF 2612 (as in 142-2); DEM 3,733 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 153; book_elev_ft: 3720; quote: Ski to the Westside Divide Junction west of Trillium Lake (see Trillium Lake Loop)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.263796" lon="-121.758805"><ele>1271.0</ele><name>Veda-Eureka saddle</name><desc>source: OSM NF 2613 node 1.61 mi from the divide, the road's local low point, DEM 4,170 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 153; book_elev_ft: 4160; quote: ski up the Sherar Burn road 1.6 miles to the Veda-Eureka saddle at 4,160 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.250757" lon="-121.776476"><ele>1346.9</ele><name>Leave the road by the pond</name><desc>source: OSM NF 2613 node 2.92 mi from the divide (1.31 from the saddle), past the road's 4,462 ft level stretch where it dips toward the pond; DEM 4,419 ft, 0.52 mi from the summit; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 153; book_elev_ft: 4470; quote: Beyond this point the road finally descends slightly, passing a small pond on the right. Anywhere along here is a good place to start up off the road (4,470 feet).</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.258098" lon="-121.774052"><ele>1518.7</ele><name>Veda Butte summit</name><desc>source: GNIS Veda Butte (summit); DEM 4,983 ft, the highest sample within 150 m; confidence: high; pdf_page: 153; book_elev_ft: 5050; quote: Ski up and northward, and climb 580 feet in 0.5 mile on a moderately steep ascending traverse to the summit</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Veda Butte (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Trillium Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Airstrip junction: osm (high), 0.48 mi | 2. Airstrip junction -&gt; Pioneer Graves junction: osm (medium), 0.52 mi | 3. Pioneer Graves junction -&gt; Westside Divide: osm (medium), 0.48 mi | 4. Westside Divide -&gt; Veda-Eureka saddle: osm (high), 1.61 mi | 5. Veda-Eureka saddle -&gt; Leave the road by the pond: osm (high), 1.30 mi | 6. Leave the road by the pond -&gt; Veda Butte summit: straight (medium), 0.52 mi</desc>
